Corporate/legal naming and presentation stay serious. The joke comes from what players do inside the serious visual system.

What this is not
PROTECT THE IDENTITY
■ Cold, clean and highly controlled.
■ Large simple shapes before surface detail.
■ Blue/white/charcoal as structural colours.
■ Fashion and editorial design influence.
■ Hard graphic character shadows inside softer environments.
AVOID DRIFTING INTO
■ Vaporwave nostalgia.
■ Frutiger Aero greenery/bubbles.
■ Generic neon cyberpunk.
■ Overly cute anime proportions.
■ Modern glossy anime-game cel shading.
■ Dense sci-fi greeble/detail for its own sake.

REFERENCE HIERARCHY
02  PRIMARY REFERENCE PLATES

These four user-selected references define the core graphic and environmental lane. They are not to be copied literally. They establish the project’s rules for colour, air, geometry, typography and visual restraint.


Reference 01 — early-2000s editorial game graphic: thin line systems, sparse copy, blue field, flare and airy negative space.
Reference 02 — Gen X Soft Club / techno-minimal composition: pale surfaces, thin geometry, sky photography, soft translucent forms.

Reference 03 — white field, sky inserts, black technical linework and abstract sculptural form. Strong example of graphic restraint.
PRIMARY WORLD REFERENCE
Reference 04 — the environmental anchor

Reference 04 — PRIMARY environmental anchor: white-blue corporate city, immaculate massing, giant graphic branding, clear roads, cobalt sky and restrained cyan accents.
This image is the strongest single environment reference for the project. The most important lesson is not “make a futuristic city”; it is how little information each building needs. White slabs, dark window bands, one large blue graphic, tiny signage and clean spacing do most of the work.
■ Take: large architectural masses, blue-white hierarchy, empty sky, polished commercial mood, billboard-scale fashion imagery, graphic branding integrated into buildings.
■ Do not take: photoreal detail density, generic sci-fi clutter, or the idea that every surface needs a futuristic prop attached to it.
■ Gameplay translation: across the tower gap, players should read as dark graphic figures against bright windows and sky rather than disappearing into noisy backgrounds.
