+# Office concept directions
+
+**Status** Target concepts for Alex's review
+
+**Last updated** 2026-11-12
+
+A bright, slightly empty corporate future frames dark-suited lawyers, a clear spiral stair and one red locked gate.
+
+Start with the [contact sheet](contact_sheet.png), with one row per direction and the four requested views in reading order.
+
+All twelve paintings were made with the built-in image generation tool.
+
+## 01 / White Trays
+
+**Broad white shelves and dark reveals make the office read as a stack of porcelain trays.**
+
+[Cutaway](01_White_Trays/cutaway.png) · [Main floor](01_White_Trays/main_floor.png) · [Rival view](01_White_Trays/rival_view.png) · [Stair](01_White_Trays/stair.png)
+
+The exterior's dominant horizontal white masses continue into low storage and flat desk islands.
+
+Thin navy glass tracks and a single cobalt wall graphic give the pale office a controlled graphic anchor.
+
+### Proposed kit work
+
+| Pieces | Proposed treatment |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Window_4m`, `Window_2m` | Develop the broad white sill shelf and shallow dark reveal from the latest window study, inside the existing sill envelope. |
+| `Column_Facade`, `Column_CornerL`, `Column_CornerR` | Recess the visible face slightly to let the horizontal white shelf read continuously, using the round-3 study's retained snap lands. |
+| Slab family | Give the existing slab edge a clean Paper White finish and a narrow navy reveal at its junction with the window band. |
+| `Wall_Solid_4m`, `Wall_Solid_2m`, `Wall_Door_4m` | White service wall, one large cobalt graphic and a restrained oversized floor identifier. |
+| `Partition_Glass_4m`, `Partition_Glass_2m` | Near-clear panes with slender navy top and base tracks. |
+| Stair family | White centre column, satin aluminium treads, tall near-clear cage and the shared radial gate proposal below. |
+
+**Proposed new material slots** `Trim_Navy` for reveals and tracks, `Accent_Cobalt` for the wall graphic, and `Light_Strip` for cool ceiling strips.
+
+The shared stair material proposals apply here too.
+
+**Proposed dimensional departures** None.
+
+## 02 / Cobalt Portal
+
+**One monumental cobalt portal frames the clear spiral against a pale, open office.**
+
+[Cutaway](02_Cobalt_Portal/cutaway.png) · [Main floor](02_Cobalt_Portal/main_floor.png) · [Rival view](02_Cobalt_Portal/rival_view.png) · [Stair](02_Cobalt_Portal/stair.png)
+
+A large squared cobalt frame is integrated into the opaque rear service wall, with a white centre behind the spiral.
+
+The portal is visible across the street, while its return at the side wall carries the graphic into the outward-looking interior view.
+
+### Proposed kit work
+
+| Pieces | Proposed treatment |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Wall_Solid_4m`, `Wall_Solid_2m`, `Wall_Door_4m` | Coordinate broad cobalt face assignments across adjacent modules to form one portal around the central white field. |
+| `Door_Leaf` | White service-door finish within the portal composition. |
+| Window and façade-column families | White sill bands and a single broad cobalt panel on an existing opaque façade area. |
+| Glass-partition family | Slim Silver Grey tracks and near-clear panes. |
+| Slab family | Ordinary pale acoustic-tile underside with sparse cool strip fixtures. |
+| Stair family | Shared white-column, aluminium-tread, clear-cage and radial-gate treatment. |
+
+**Proposed new material slots** `Accent_Cobalt` for coordinated large wall faces, `Trim_Navy` for restrained reveals and `Light_Strip` for ceiling fixtures.
+
+The portal can be authored with face assignments or a coherent large graphic across modules.
+
+**Proposed dimensional departures** None.
+
+The portal's depth belongs to the existing opaque wall surfaces, keeping the open circulation around the cage.
+
+## 03 / Luminous Grid
+
+**A field of large luminous ceiling squares turns everyday office tiles into a calm artificial sky.**
+
+[Cutaway](03_Luminous_Grid/cutaway.png) · [Main floor](03_Luminous_Grid/main_floor.png) · [Rival view](03_Luminous_Grid/rival_view.png) · [Stair](03_Luminous_Grid/stair.png)
+
+Broad luminous squares alternate with ordinary acoustic tiles to give the office a recognisable ceiling silhouette.
+
+The square order continues into quiet carpet zones and rectilinear furniture, with one cobalt square on the service wall.
+
+### Proposed kit work
+
+| Pieces | Proposed treatment |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Slab_2x2`, `Slab_4x2`, `Slab_2x4`, `Slab_4x4` | Coordinate the underside into a 2 m luminous/acoustic field, with thin Silver Grey divisions. |
+| Proposed `Ceiling_Light_2x2` visual module | A flush luminous face for a light-cell variant, integrated at the 4.3 m soffit. |
+| `Slab_Stairwell` | Carry the ceiling order to the circular stair opening and trim the interrupted cells to its edge. |
+| Wall family | Paper White faces with one large cobalt square and a small floor identifier. |
+| Window and glass-partition families | White sills, restrained navy reveals, Silver Grey tracks and near-clear glass. |
+| Stair family | Shared white-column, aluminium-tread, clear-cage and radial-gate treatment. |
+
+**Proposed new material slots** `Ceiling_Luminous` for the broad cool-white light cells, `Accent_Cobalt` for the wall square, and `Trim_Navy` for the window reveals.
+
+Use the existing `Ceiling_Tile` material for the acoustic cells and `Frame_Aluminium` for thin divisions.
+
+**Proposed dimensional departures** None.
+
+The light faces sit at the 4.3 m soffit.
+
+The cutaway retains a thin roof section to show their underside.
+
+## Shared construction proposals
+
+The [kit README](../../README.md) supplies the construction dimensions and existing piece names.
+
+The [request](REQUEST.md) supplies the concept layout.
+
+The reference floor-plan sketch depicts an older 20 m-wide floor, a 10 m main area and rear stairs.
+
+The request and current blockout govern the 28 m-wide floor and centre-back spiral used here.
+
+| Element | Construction target |
+| --- | --- |
+| Floor | 28 m wide, 14 m open main floor and 4 m rear service spine. |
+| Front | Seven 4 m bays with 1 m opaque cover sills and uninterrupted clear glass above. |
+| Heights | 4.3 m clear soffit, 4.5 m floor spacing and 0.2 m slab. |
+| Stair | Centre about 10 m behind the façade, one full turn per floor, treads out to 2.6 m radius. |
+| Centre column | 0.8 m radius, following the kit's explicit measurement. |
+| Cage | Tall flat clear panels at the kit's 2.75 m radius, with an open arrival gap. |
+| Meeting rooms | 2.5 m high clear partitions, open above to the ceiling. |
+| Service rooms | Three opaque rooms, WC / STORE / UTIL, with 1.2 × 2.4 m door openings. |
+| Rival | Matching floor heights and façade rhythm across the 12 m street gap. |
+
+I interpreted the request's “0.8 m white column” using the kit's explicit radius.
+
+The kit's suggested 8 / 12 / 8 m service-room split guided the cutaways.
+
+The roof and front glazing are selectively cut away in the dollhouse paintings to expose the layout.
+
+### Stair finishes and gate
+
+**Proposed `Stair_PaperWhite` slot** gives `Stair_Column` its white finish, while `Stair_Flight` uses `Stair_Aluminium`.
+
+**Proposed `Door_LockedRed` slot** reserves the strong red finish for the stair's closed gate.
+
+**Proposed `Stair_Gate_Radial` visual variant** places the hinge at the centre column and the latch at the outer cage, just after the arrival gap.
+
+The radial walking width is approximately 1.8 m from the 2.6 m tread radius minus the 0.8 m column radius, before frame allowances.
+
+The existing `Door_Leaf` is 1.18 m wide, so the gate needs its own reviewed visual variant to span that path.
+
+The paintings explore a sloping gate silhouette that follows the stair composition.
+
+Final gate framing and leaf shape are an approval item for the selected direction.
+
+All proposed slots and pieces are concept-stage production suggestions.
+
+## Image attempts
+
+A try means one image-generation call, including a targeted correction.
+
+| Direction | Cutaway | Main floor | Rival view | Stair | Total |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| White Trays | 3 | 2 | 3 | 2 | 10 |
+| Cobalt Portal | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 5 |
+| Luminous Grid | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 5 |
+| **Total** | **7** | **4** | **5** | **4** | **20** |
+
+White Trays' first cutaway had an extra service-room divider, which was removed.
+
+Early rival views exposed legs below the specified cover height, and a correction introduced extra horizontal bands.
+
+The delivered rival view was regenerated with a single continuous opaque sill band per floor.
+
+The stair close-up was revised to show an open entry and a gate across the radial stair path.
+
+That gate arrangement was carried into the remaining White Trays and Cobalt Portal views.
+
+Luminous Grid's cutaway was revised to reduce the ceiling section's thickness and align its gate.
+
+The [generation record](generation_prompts.json) contains the prompt for every attempt and the final image counts.
+
+## Resolution and visual review
+
+The tool returned every painting at 1672 × 941 despite requests for the largest native landscape output.
+
+Each final image is 1664 × 936, exact 16:9, using a centred crop of four pixels on each side, two at the top and three at the bottom.
+
+The images retain their native pixel scale.
+
+The contact sheet is 3960 × 2088 and uses twelve 960 × 540 thumbnails.
+
+The sheet was composed with PowerShell and System.Drawing.
+
+All twelve delivered paintings and the assembled sheet were visually inspected.
+
+The review covered the central stair, three-room spine, open meeting-room glazing, cover sills, coarse bay divisions, red gate, suit visibility and the absence of decorative plants.
+
+### Visual limitations
+
+The paintings' carpet has more visible mottling than the bible's low-noise material target.
+
+**Suggestion** use a restrained grey-blue carpet material with subtle tile seams when the selected direction is modelled.
+
+Painted perspective, tread spacing, gate framing and glass-panel faceting vary between views.
+
+Exact radii, camera height, street distance and floor spacing need metric verification against the kit during modelling.
+
+The generated clear-glass appearance provides a visual target for a future material.
+
+Unity material response and cross-tower gameplay readability require direct observation in the game.
+
+### Static file verification
+
+The following PowerShell checks ran from the repository root.
+
+```powershell
+Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Drawing
+$officeConceptFolders = @('01_White_Trays','02_Cobalt_Portal','03_Luminous_Grid')
+$officeAssetCount = 0
+$officeInvalidCount = 0
+foreach ($officeConceptFolder in $officeConceptFolders) {
+    foreach ($officeShotName in @('cutaway','main_floor','rival_view','stair')) {
+        $officeFile = Get-Item -LiteralPath ('ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Office/' + $officeConceptFolder + '/' + $officeShotName + '.png')
+        $officeAsset = [System.Drawing.Image]::FromFile($officeFile.FullName)
+        if ($officeAsset.Width -ne 1664 -or $officeAsset.Height -ne 936 -or $officeAsset.Width * 9 -ne $officeAsset.Height * 16) { $officeInvalidCount++ }
+        $officeAssetCount++
+        $officeAsset.Dispose()
+    }
+}
+$officeSheetAsset = [System.Drawing.Image]::FromFile((Resolve-Path -LiteralPath 'ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Office/contact_sheet.png'))
+Write-Output "Concept images $officeAssetCount, invalid sizes $officeInvalidCount, contact sheet $($officeSheetAsset.Width)x$($officeSheetAsset.Height)"
+$officeSheetAsset.Dispose()
+$officeArchive = Get-Content -Encoding UTF8 -LiteralPath 'ArtSource/Kit/concepts/Office/generation_prompts.json' -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
+Write-Output "Prompt records $($officeArchive.prompts.Count), image records $($officeArchive.images.Count), summed tries $(($officeArchive.images | Measure-Object -Property tries -Sum).Sum)"
+```
+
+Observed results were 12 concept images, zero invalid sizes, a 3960 × 2088 contact sheet, 20 prompt records, 12 image records and 20 summed tries.
